========
OVERVIEW
========

OFELIA Control Framework's virtualization agent (OXA) has been sucessfully
ported to CentOS 5.x. Other components may follow, based on demand. There
are currently no plans to port any components to CentOS 6.x, as XEN has
was deprecated in this release and major work in backporting is required.


===============
PRE-PREQUISITES
===============

-> CentOS 5.x installed (with or without graphical interface)

-> XEN platform installed; XEN kernel installed and booted

-> Extra repositories:

    -> Extra Packages for Enterprise Linux (EPEL)
    
        wget http://dl.fedoraproject.org/pub/epel/5/i386/epel-release-5-4.noarch.rpm
        rpm -Uvh epel-release-5*.rpm
        
    ->  IUS Community Project (IUS)
    
        wget dl.iuscommunity.org/pub/ius/stable/Redhat/5/i386/ius-release-1.0-10.ius.el5.noarch.rpm
        rpm -Uvh ius-release-*.rpm
        
    ->  FIBRE-UFSCAR Repo (temporary location)
    
        wget http://www2.comp.ufscar.br/~ricardofg/centos5/fibre-ufscar.repo -O /etc/yum.repos.d/
        
        
-> Package "rhel-lsb" must be installed

    yum install rhel-lsb


============
INSTALLATION
============

Installing OXA on CentOS is a strightforward process, identical to installing
it on Debian:

mkdir -p /opt/ofelia/oxa/repository
cd /opt/ofelia
# (clone this repository to have a copy of all component's directories here)
cd oxa/repository
# (again, clone this repository to have a copy of all components here)
cd vt_manager/src/python/agent/tools/
ofver install -f


